From b4ce01b03e0462619f5bb278a7ce52f5a0749486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneplus-nord2t-karen contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 03:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: fix control build type errors

Give the OPlus foreground-boost declaration its actual void return type.
Also restore the node deferred-split pointer assignment described by the
adjacent source comment; the published line assigned an integer address to a
different pointer field and does not compile with the pinned Lineage clang.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
---
 kernel/sched/extension/eas_plus.c | 2 +-
 mm/page_alloc.c                   | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/extension/eas_plus.c b/kernel/sched/extension/eas_plus.c
index 7fd48dc..8307566 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/extension/eas_plus.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/extension/eas_plus.c
@@ -295 +295 @@
-extern oplus_task_sched_boost(struct task_struct *p, int *task_prefer);
+extern void oplus_task_sched_boost(struct task_struct *p, int *task_prefer);
diff --git a/mm/page_alloc.c b/mm/page_alloc.c
index 133135c..00996f4 100644
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -7074 +7074 @@
-	chp_lruvec->ds = (unsigned long)chp_lruvec; // pgdat->split_queue_len;
+	pgdat->split_queue_len = (unsigned long)chp_lruvec;
--
2.51.0
